/* HIRED_RAW: hired swords and Dramatis Personae. They do not count toward warrior or hero limits.
   Fields:
     id      unique id (warbands can refer to it in hireOnly / noHire)
     n       name           race  race key (see races.js)
     st      nine stats as one string: "M WS BS S T W I A Ld"
     c       hire fee       up    upkeep per battle        rt  rating added
     src     book or source g     grade key (see grades.js)
     sk      skill list keys, space separated    spells  spell list keys (optional)
     kit     text describing starting gear, shown as written
     hireAlt / upAlt   only for the rare sword paid in something other than gold crowns
             (Wyrdstone shards, Treasures). Text shown in place of the gold figure, e.g.
             "1 Wyrdstone shard per game". Leave c/up at 0 for these so the treasury isn't
             also charged gold for the same fee. Don't use this for a cost this tool has no
             other way to track (campaign points, for instance) where a real gold figure is
             still being charged - note that in the note field instead so the display matches
             what actually happens to the treasury
     note    special rules text, in full. Where it covers more than one named rule, write it as
             "Name: text. Name2: text2." (same convention as a weapon's wd in equipment.js) and
             the tool shows each one on its own line, named in bold, instead of one run-on
             paragraph. rules ties in the same shared special rules used everywhere else (Fear,
             Large Target, Immune to Psychology, and so on, see data/rules.js); use it instead of
             retyping a rule this sword already carries
     kitItems  the kit's items as a list of exact names from equipment.js (weapons, armour, and
             other gear alike). Where matched automatically, a name may appear more than once
             (e.g. ["Axe","Axe"] for "two axes"). Armour items here count toward the save shown
             on the card, and weapons show their Strength/range/save-penalty line from
             equipment.js. A handful of kits are unique enough (bare-handed fighters, named
             magic weapons, animal claws) that nothing is listed; the kit text still describes
             them.
     kitOptions  choices the player makes when hiring, for example a choice of weapons:
             [{"n":"Weapons","list":[{"n":"Two axes"},{"n":"Double-handed axe"}]}]
             The first option is the default. An option may also carry txt (text shown in the kit line),
             kitItems (armour that counts for the save), sv (a save it gives) and rt (rating it adds).
     kitBase text for the fixed part of the kit, shown after the chosen options (used with kitOptions)
     sv      fixed armour save                    noXp  true if it never gains experience
   Hiring rules use warband ids and tags:
     only:[...]  only these warbands or tags may hire it     not:[...]  these may not hire it
     excl:[...]  never in the same warband as these swords */
